WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.740
If your prep is MiraLAX, this video will walk you through exactly how to take

2
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:03.840
it.

3
00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.080
Just follow along step by step.

4
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:10.700
For this prep, you'll need a few items, all available over the counter, no

5
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:11.600
prescription needed.

6
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.160
You'll need one 238 gram bottle of MiraLAX powder,

7
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:21.040
two to four Dulcolax laxative tablets, and 64 ounces of a clear sports drink

8
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:21.840
like Gatorade,

9
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:26.460
Propel, or Crystal Light. That's usually two 32 ounce bottles. If you have

10
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:26.720
diabetes,

11
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:32.010
use sugar free Gatorade G2. Also, make sure you get the laxative tablets, not

12
00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:33.040
the stool softener.

13
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:38.560
One important rule, your sports drink cannot be red, orange, blue, or purple.

14
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:43.550
Stick to clear or light colored flavors. The day before your colonoscopy, you

15
00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:44.480
'll start by mixing

16
00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:49.540
the solution. Pour the entire bottle of MiraLAX into a pitcher with all 64

17
00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:50.720
ounces of the sports

18
00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:55.310
drink. Stir or shake until the powder is completely dissolved. You can chill it

19
00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:56.160
in the refrigerator

20
00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.800
if you'd like, keeping it cold makes it easier to drink.

21
00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:05.460
Now for part one, the evening before your procedure. At 5 p.m., take your Dulcolax

22
00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:06.080
tablets

23
00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:09.680
with a glass of water. Your doctor's instructions will tell you whether to take

24
00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:10.400
two or four,

25
00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.980
follow their guidance on the specific amount. At 6 p.m., you'll start drinking

26
00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:15.600
the first half of

27
00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.430
the solution. That's 32 ounces. Drink an eight ounce glass every 15 minutes

28
00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:21.440
until that half is

29
00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:26.490
gone. Keep drinking clear liquids after you finish. For part two, six hours

30
00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:27.040
before your

31
00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:31.660
colonoscopy, you'll drink the second half, which is another 32 ounces. Drink

32
00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:33.280
this at the same pace,

33
00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:38.110
an eight ounce glass every 15 minutes. You can continue to have clear liquids

34
00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:38.480
up until

35
00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:43.120
four hours before your procedure. This part is really important. You must drink

36
00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:43.760
all of the prep

37
00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:47.760
solution as directed, even if you're already passing clear liquid. I know it

38
00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:48.560
can feel like

39
00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:52.550
enough, but finishing the entire dose is what gives us the clearest view during

40
00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:53.200
your procedure.

41
00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:58.030
If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may need to reschedule, and neither

42
00:01:58.030 --> 00:01:58.800
of us wants that.

43
00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:03.390
Please drink plenty of liquids throughout the process to prevent dehydration.

44
00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:04.240
Staying

45
00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:08.040
hydrated will help you feel better and help the prep do its job. If you

46
00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:10.000
experience any discomfort

47
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.800
from frequent trips to the bathroom, applying a petroleum-based ointment or

48
00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.800
diaper rash cream

49
00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:20.780
can really help. That's it. You've got this. Follow the timing, finish the full

50
00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:21.920
dose, and stay hydrated.

51
00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:26.510
If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office. We're here

52
00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:27.120
to help.
